THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
These are not owned by the copyright holder; their own licenses and notices apply:
  - games/flags/flags/*.svg — flag-icons by lipis (https://github.com/lipis/flag-icons),
    MIT License, see games/flags/flags/LICENSE.
  - games/flags/countries.json — derived from mledoze/countries (https://github.com/mledoze/countries),
    Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0, see games/flags/ATTRIBUTION.txt.
  - games/boggle/words/ru.json — noun list from Harrix/Russian-Nouns
    (https://github.com/Harrix/Russian-Nouns), MIT License; word frequencies from "The New Frequency
    Dictionary of Russian Vocabulary" by O. N. Lyashevskaya and S. A. Sharov (2009).
  - games/wordle/words/*.json — word lists compiled from publicly available sources; they belong to
    their respective owners.
  - games/chess/engine.js — the piece-square table values follow the "Simplified Evaluation
    Function" by Tomasz Michniewski, published on the Chess Programming Wiki
    (https://www.chessprogramming.org/Simplified_Evaluation_Function).
  - games/go/engine.js — the 3x3 playout patterns follow the MoGo patterns (S. Gelly, Y. Wang, R. Munos,
    O. Teytaud, "Modification of UCT with Patterns in Monte-Carlo Go", 2006) in the form listed by the
    michi engine by Petr Baudis (https://github.com/pasky/michi, MIT License); the search parameters
    (RAVE equivalence, prior values) are inspired by michi. The code itself is original.
  - styles/fonts/press-start-2p-*.woff2 — the "Press Start 2P" font by CodeMan38
    (Copyright 2012 The Press Start 2P Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1,
    see styles/fonts/OFL-press-start-2p.txt.
  - styles/fonts/golos-text-*.woff2 — the "Golos Text" font (Copyright 2019 The Golos Text Project
    Authors, https://github.com/googlefonts/golos-text), SIL Open Font License 1.1,
    see styles/fonts/OFL-golos-text.txt.
  - games/nonogram/levels.js — the pictures of the "Вкусное" levels are derived from "16x16 Food" by
    ARoachIFoundOnMyPillow (https://opengameart.org/content/16x16-food), CC0 1.0; the "Зверята" levels — from
    "Tiny Creatures" by Clint Bellanger (https://clintbellanger.net), CC0 1.0; the "Эмодзи" and "Большие
    картинки" levels — from Microsoft Fluent Emoji (https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji),
    Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation, MIT License, see games/nonogram/LICENSE-fluent-emoji.txt. The pictures
    were reduced to puzzle grids; the "Разминка" pictures are original.
  - games/arkanoid/levels.js — the brick layouts follow the levels of Ricochet Xtreme (Reflexive
    Entertainment, 2001) as recreated in the fan level set "Ricochet Xtreme Homage" by Alf and BigMama
    (https://www.ricochetuniverse.com); the layouts belong to their respective owners. Only brick positions
    and kinds are used; the code, graphics, sounds and bonus behaviour of the game are original.
  - The Telegram Web App script is loaded from telegram.org at runtime and is not part of this
    repository.

The rules and mechanics of well-known game genres (2048, sudoku, mahjong solitaire, checkers, chess,
